 and digital collage techniques"}], "description": "Students learn how fragments produce meaning."}, {"id": "c1351fef-9c0a-4606-a749-98b6ec9af2ac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Narrative and atmosphere", "children": [{"id": "426a6ecf-519a-4cea-aa7d-c1628adac804", "type": "concept", "title": "Storyboarding, speculative scenes, material mood, cultural context, and memory"}, {"id": "82138d0a-16aa-433d-a317-93ca797f819f", "type": "concept", "title": "Time, weather, occupation, and change"}, {"id": "d3b042fa-0824-48f2-91e4-d73be2d6d9a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding empty mood-board aesthetics"}], "description": "The point is to represent possible worlds and design intentions."}, {"id": "d6d52e49-cd6a-4540-9df9-355c5433ae2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-media experimentation", "children": [{"id": "8dc48784-03dc-4c6e-9504-df21999ac7f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphite, charcoal, ink, pastel, colored pencil, print, photography, transfer, paint, and digital overlays"}, {"id": "4df2bb0e-3191-4523-a69f-798082d8c5ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Large-scale drawing and installation-like presentation"}, {"id": "ef029ad8-00fd-4089-9c34-8ae2d5da15bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Material choices as conceptual decisions"}], "description": "Students expand the representational palette."}]}, {"id": "e3c82477-4e9a-4cbb-abc2-446225cae36c", "type": "topic", "title": "Rendering Techniques: Light, Shadow, Material, Color, Texture, Atmosphere, and Post-Production", "description": "This topic develops rendering judgment across hand, digital, and hybrid techniques, emphasizing legibility, mood, materiality, and restraint.", "children": [{"id": "28d397c9-2c37-41cc-99e5-2eaad4b0286f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Light and shadow", "children": [{"id": "16711f3c-323f-4d0a-a621-ed651361f864", "type": "concept", "title": "Sun angle, artificial light, ambient light, cast shadow, shade, reflection, and glow"}, {"id": "46359469-124d-4847-a001-2e9c4009f25e", "type": "concept", "title": "Value structure and focus"}, {"id": "f50c8403-57e5-479b-b342-1237f1fca147", "type": "concept", "title": "Day/night and seasonal conditions"}], "description": "Students learn that rendering begins with light logic."}, {"id": "c3deee3b-0c0a-45f7-8849-79c2483d713a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Material and color", "children": [{"id": "f566121e-4462-4096-a03c-140663c3e345", "type": "concept", "title": "Wood, concrete, brick, metal, glass, fabric, vegetation, water, and ground"}, {"id": "395bccbb-0f0d-4ec6-9e9d-83d7a4521f79", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture scale, bump, reflection, color temperature, and weathering"}, {"id": "10a128b7-f63e-4fa0-b5f3-24018637cad8", "type": "concept", "title": "Color palettes and restraint"}], "description": "The gist is to communicate material character without visual clutter."}, {"id": "4abd5e55-0f49-4604-84ee-d51738b35e03", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Post-production", "children": [{"id": "ca37891e-17f6-458a-92f0-78a8b63ad453", "type": "concept", "title": "Compositing, masks, entourage, atmosphere, correction, sharpening, noise, and output size"}, {"id": "34d864f7-de87-41e4-9a84-c16b9c146ef3", "type": "concept", "title": "Rendering over model exports and linework"}, {"id": "c1218e88-baa0-41e1-9cbe-9c6d9c284953", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding deceptive or overproduced images"}], "description": "Students refine images for clarity and argument."}]}, {"id": "5b9f201e-028b-4ff6-a73e-b59d451bb26b", "type": "topic", "title": "Photography for Architects: Site, Model, Process, Precedent, and Image Editing", "description": "Students learn photography as a representation tool for documenting site, models, materials, process, and final work.", "children": [{"id": "acc5525d-19b6-431d-8866-d2c52e51ba0c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Site photography", "children": [{"id": "6a136e5a-aa4f-4b2b-9207-cec808578390", "type": "concept", "title": "Light, view sequence, approach, use patterns, materials, edges, and details"}, {"id": "c83c11df-add9-43b7-a2b0-42d09917ca52", "type": "concept", "title": "Panoramas, serial views, and photo maps"}, {"id": "513b2975-5ffc-452e-bf7b-8c729b2f776c", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata, captions, and source discipline"}], "description": "Students learn to document context as evidence."}, {"id": "6e2c81b8-2d90-4221-90e3-85c6241575d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Model and process photography", "children": [{"id": "cb3afa2e-7294-4f88-80f7-d4e1edb9fe97", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting setup, background, focus, depth of field, scale figures, and shadows"}, {"id": "01d3a439-90ff-43c9-9960-c60dddd9e763", "type": "concept", "title": "Process documentation and iteration records"}, {"id": "7665a4e9-ff32-4536-8d7d-d31fc97cc411", "type": "concept", "title": "Cropping and file management"}], "description": "The point is to make physical work legible in critique and portfolio."}, {"id": "4722713c-632e-41f0-a2cf-704dcac24df4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image editing", "children": [{"id": "a5a0d379-9670-4f27-8b7c-4f51ba409b15", "type": "concept", "title": "Exposure, white balance, perspective correction, cleanup, color, and sequencing"}, {"id": "23dfa2ed-8b85-49c9-abdf-7881bef6b33d", "type": "concept", "title": "Composite reference images and site overlays"}, {"id": "3f4a240f-b541-4ecd-960e-e744f1e06d78", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical limits of manipulation"}], "description": "Students edit photographs responsibly for representation."}]}, {"id": "2674425e-f114-410e-8163-376846a3e542", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Modeling to Drawing: Geometry, Views, Exports, Linework, Layout, and Version Control", "description": "This module connects three-dimensional model thinking to precise two-dimensional drawings and repeatable studio workflows.", "children": [{"id": "5b2f1792-f1a6-4fed-9d61-12fed758da38", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Model organization", "children": [{"id": "5032142d-8271-46da-a8a1-9b5d42bc0126", "type": "concept", "title": "Layers, groups, blocks, components, naming, units, coordinates, and model hygiene"}, {"id": "e8db2529-598d-4a3d-ba8c-a69973713d9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Surface, solid, and mesh logic"}, {"id": "63d0d0e7-78b0-458b-8ad8-f4107e0bed6b", "type": "concept", "title": "Model scope and level of detail"}], "description": "Students learn to build digital models that can generate useful drawings."}, {"id": "9b3dd0f6-d22a-483d-9847-ef688e6ff916", "type": "subtopic", "title": "View extraction", "children": [{"id": "03ed4c37-8736-4da7-8be2-2cdafc518d0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Plans, sections, elevations, axonometrics, perspectives, clipping planes, and make2D/export workflows"}, {"id": "1f29b02b-6e5b-445a-8025-4423388fe24e", "type": "concept", "title": "Linework cleanup and hierarchy"}, {"id": "674ddd14-1062-40e8-bd7f-f1705619833c", "type": "concept", "title": "Model-to-layout coordination"}], "description": "The gist is to translate models into clear architectural drawings."}, {"id": "dacd9dff-dc7b-4fc0-b2e9-b7e78a1af1f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Version control habits", "children": [{"id": "e7dfe495-e57a-4bf5-8b96-c2046c13119c", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming, dated versions, backups, linked files, package folders, and export records"}, {"id": "0131c3d3-4c15-452e-9e50-3764bfb70adf", "type": "concept", "title": "Iteration logs and review submissions"}, {"id": "08f3419e-7fa2-4fe1-97ad-601a67abb5f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Collaboration and authorship clarity"}], "description": "Students protect design work from chaos."}]}, {"id": "cbfcc5e9-d3ad-4c65-9706-69531b99b7f5", "type": "topic", "title": "Large-Scale, Experimental, and Atmospheric Drawing", "description": "Students expand drawing beyond small exercises into immersive, atmospheric, and exploratory formats that can stand as design research.", "children": [{"id": "1b4d3a5c-924c-47e1-9c7a-25e06cf007c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scale shift", "children": [{"id": "465d5824-7c9c-4ada-8b64-53923314d9a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Wall drawings, scrolls, composite sheets, oversized perspectives, and room-scale maps"}, {"id": "ce4829c8-4187-48dd-8c36-27910105d711", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture, movement, and material force"}, {"id": "be7c9360-c2c6-437b-bfde-d5ce68c04250", "type": "concept", "title": "Viewing distance and installation context"}], "description": "Students learn how large drawings change body, gesture, and interpretation."}, {"id": "3b223499-aaa6-4611-b2d8-8a9e99eef298", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Atmospheric drawing", "children": [{"id": "523ba696-0d08-40af-8960-f259c97455cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Air, light, sound, weather, time, occupation, memory, and mood"}, {"id": "fa1ce46d-593e-489e-a34f-9574c57ce584", "type": "concept", "title": "Soft edges, gradients, erasure, layering, and ambiguity"}, {"id": "23c40e3d-f96b-41bf-b6ee-98994c0fe20c", "type": "concept", "title": "Atmosphere tied to architectural intention"}], "description": "The point is to represent qualities that technical drawings often miss."}, {"id": "43760601-6891-4010-a67d-f5f5f8f78850", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Drawing as final work", "children": [{"id": "438d9473-ad1f-47e4-b451-2754ed5ac9ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Series, sequencing, conceptual consistency, craft, and exhibition"}, {"id": "415382d2-9176-458a-b424-f767da9de45b", "type": "concept", "title": "Drawing independent of building proposal"}, {"id": "15d27c30-635e-46d5-918c-c2d998099fa0", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique criteria for experimental work"}], "description": "Students treat drawing as a complete design artifact."}]}, {"id": "3ec1f91a-a339-4573-ba2c-09c4ff0ff091", "type": "topic", "title": "Graphic Hierarchy, Annotation, Typography, Color Systems, and Presentation Composition", "description": "This topic builds communication discipline so drawings, labels, images, and layouts guide an audience clearly through a project.", "children": [{"id": "20aa6f56-921e-4859-9581-12578422df06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hierarchy and layout", "children": [{"id": "e97fb3a4-a4da-4508-955f-d2f45ee84279", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary, secondary, and tertiary information"}, {"id": "f9db457f-e139-4d1f-b6f6-e26b9a546d39", "type": "concept", "title": "Margins, grids, alignment, spacing, scale, and white space"}, {"id": "dd314372-2e91-4e67-9d23-40835027ff6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Board composition and narrative flow"}], "description": "Students learn to guide the viewer's eye."}, {"id": "1873b4c7-b906-40fa-ac19-9d6e8663f9ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Annotation and typography", "children": [{"id": "74b357fd-e40a-4bbc-a98f-17cc012dcfc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Titles, labels, callouts, legends, scale bars, captions, and notes"}, {"id": "26a7977b-e247-4886-8e12-c61236f2a3c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Type pairing, size, weight, tracking, and consistency"}, {"id": "303d6d61-c6d3-4561-83ed-6abebca97aa3", "type": "concept", "title": "Writing less but saying more"}], "description": "The gist is to use text as part of representation."}, {"id": "a9edf3c1-c85a-4593-9ae8-aec8e3551366", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color systems", "children": [{"id": "190d514b-7880-405e-aea2-2bdd179f9326", "type": "concept", "title": "Limited palettes, coding systems, contrast, accessibility, material color, and atmospheric color"}, {"id": "732d5ac1-675f-44ad-bb1d-e98904fa7baf", "type": "concept", "title": "Color for analysis versus color for mood"}, {"id": "dfdcd0a0-c1e2-42b9-9367-7a306f96291a", "type": "concept", "title": "Print and screen calibration"}], "description": "Students use color deliberately."}]}, {"id": "aa7e08b6-2db6-4dd2-8bf6-8f75d638534b", "type": "topic", "title": "Portfolio Visualization: Editing, Sequencing, Project Narrative, Boards, and Review Culture", "description": "Students learn how representation choices shape portfolio identity, critique performance, and the public life of a design project.", "children": [{"id": "775dc0c9-9f9d-4b38-b1fe-a5d51020e24e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project editing", "children": [{"id": "dd911c8c-5334-47ac-bd6a-38c56f652a42", "type": "concept", "title": "Choosing key drawings, removing redundancy, identifying gaps, and improving weak images"}, {"id": "c8072f8e-ed52-4662-b3a8-000e33c7979f", "type": "concept", "title": "Process versus final work balance"}, {"id": "ec99c876-3d75-4310-b571-01e3bd85ca0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience and purpose"}], "description": "Students learn that portfolios are made by selection as much as production."}, {"id": "35b911b4-23bb-49eb-a534-4d95d918c75b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sequencing and narrative", "children": [{"id": "3bf58692-6fc3-44b7-9b5a-ae0418a7c7c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Opening image, concept, context, process, plans/sections, experiential views, details, and closing image"}, {"id": "ebf5c41f-e68a-4dc3-8004-ff4f7e194033", "type": "concept", "title": "Page rhythm and transitions"}, {"id": "0bec05be-facb-49f5-895c-a757d451e3ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Captions and argument"}], "description": "The point is to make a project understandable across pages."}, {"id": "177c2bd0-1537-48e3-8495-47041165cfe0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Review culture", "children": [{"id": "a8fa7c2b-7e32-4505-80c1-c9e3ca4fb3fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Board hierarchy, verbal presentation, critique notes, revisions, and documentation"}, {"id": "7dd62d39-f476-4011-ac76-ef82ac33197d", "type": "concept", "title": "Time management and production schedule"}, {"id": "ac9f027c-1c8a-4633-8908-b3f40e09b9a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Resilience and iteration after feedback"}], "description": "Students prepare work for critique, pin-up, and portfolio review."}]}, {"id": "eef99666-2083-4a9a-a785-df3900e1263c", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics and Limits of Architectural Visualization: Evidence, Persuasion, AI, Context, and Responsibility", "description": "This module asks students to represent design honestly while recognizing that images can clarify, persuade, obscure, or mislead.", "children": [{"id": "69a17cbf-c54d-471e-ac91-6512a4c46a26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Truth and persuasion", "children": [{"id": "277f45c9-63ed-4f52-aa40-9ca36e6064bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Selective framing, idealized users, unrealistic lighting, hidden context, and speculative promises"}, {"id": "8ec78fe5-a9e6-42c7-8386-4f30b646783c", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-based visualization"}, {"id": "e8ca9e04-8b78-4c50-91bc-8d312a4c89a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Disclosing assumptions and limits"}], "description": "Students examine how images shape belief about a project."}, {"id": "f47d5a72-b458-41c1-8529-152b2f35f6e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and inclusion", "children": [{"id": "847123da-90ef-4b0b-be9d-9d59a02a9d37", "type": "concept", "title": "Entourage diversity, accessibility, publicness, gender, age, race, class, and cultural context"}, {"id": "3ee3b300-f135-42d1-bad0-ed98bde22330", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding tokenism and extractive imagery"}, {"id": "bce06f20-5567-4370-95a6-795edbc686e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Community-sensitive representation"}], "description": "The gist is to ask who is shown, omitted, or stereotyped."}, {"id": "a09a40b4-7d60-4a00-bf88-8291d85d7741", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emerging tools", "children": [{"id": "9ba54d69-74ff-4369-b63b-0092cbbcbf8f", "type": "concept", "title": "AI image generation, model-based rendering, asset libraries, and post-production shortcuts"}, {"id": "b25740ed-0072-4e26-a73e-f4c084a4132d", "type": "concept", "title": "Authorship, copyright, bias, and studio integrity"}, {"id": "99d70136-95ed-4ab0-abde-8ec3c27d5b6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Tool use policies and transparent workflows"}], "description": "Students evaluate AI and automated visualization critically."}]}, {"id": "8152afa9-f117-488e-8296-c3a1dd47a8e5", "type": "topic", "title": "Final Project Visualization Package: Integrated Drawing, Rendering, Diagram, Photography, and Portfolio Spread", "description": "Students synthesize the course in a complete visual package that communicates concept, process, site, space, material, and atmosphere.", "children": [{"id": "c94b099f-70c1-4693-b622-49f05e9cbbd1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Package strategy", "children": [{"id": "47cba369-2d38-4303-b56e-3d2a802de3ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept, site, program, form, section, atmosphere, material, process, and user experience"}, {"id": "ee6dfeff-725a-4a5d-a4b1-578e437d7334", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience, format, and review criteria"}, {"id": "c5c52bc3-7f48-4d69-8286-1957010549ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Production schedule and priorities"}], "description": "Students define what the final visual package must communicate."}, {"id": "0761e3ad-766d-4073-aead-4076d0babb16", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrated deliverables", "children": [{"id": "29f6762e-4188-45ca-b07f-6ca22b7cbe42", "type": "concept", "title": "Plans, sections, diagrams, perspectives, renderings, collages, photographs, and detail views"}, {"id": "17a3b545-0f59-44d4-af5b-10d0161928a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistent linework, palette, typography, and annotation"}, {"id": "c76da246-7e0c-427d-94cb-0fd9d4996624", "type": "concept", "title": "Analog/digital craft and quality control"}], "description": "The point is to make different media work together."}, {"id": "35f77ffb-33ac-4772-aa84-8c08af025ee0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final critique and revision", "children": [{"id": "220977db-9d23-440b-9a39-ce46557a059e", "type": "concept", "title": "Pin-up presentation, peer critique, instructor comments, self-assessment, and revision plan"}, {"id": "d8d2a39a-2705-4a08-91f7-949956542878", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio-ready export and archive"}, {"id": "6e96afe2-c0eb-44c2-9b92-f126fb00e285", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflection on representation as design research"}], "description": "Students learn to improve representation through feedback."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$vr2json$::jsonb,
